{{!
	One entry of data-page-aside.array-flow-panels or array-sticky-panels:
	the chrome every panel but the table of contents shares, in either zone.
	Root, heading and body are direct children in that order; the body holds
	the panel's own partial, opened on its `body` data. Dispatch is static
	because MediaWiki's TemplateParser cannot resolve a partial name from
	data, so a new panel costs one line inside the body.
	string panel-id
	string panel-label
	number panel-order position within its zone; scripts place their own against it
	bool has-panel-module whether a script fills the body
	string panel-module the ResourceLoader module that fills it; the client
		registry reads it to drop the frame if that module fails
	bool is-<panel-id>
	object body the panel's own template data
	The body holds no whitespace, so a body no partial fills is :empty — the
	hook a wiki styles a declared panel's placeholder on.
}}
<div id="citizen-page-aside-{{panel-id}}" class="citizen-page-aside__panel citizen-page-aside__panel--{{panel-id}}" data-order="{{panel-order}}"{{#has-panel-module}} data-module="{{panel-module}}"{{/has-panel-module}}>
	<div id="citizen-page-aside-{{panel-id}}-heading" class="citizen-page-aside__heading">{{panel-label}}</div>
	<div class="citizen-page-aside__body">{{#is-lastmod}}{{#body}}{{>PageAsidePanel__lastmod}}{{/body}}{{/is-lastmod}}</div>
</div>
